{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 52, :comments ["<b>His years</b> — three times [in the Masorah]: דין (here), and the other two: ורב שיהיו ימי שניו, מספר שניו ולא יחקר. Meaning: according to his years, whether they are many, as written: ורב שיהיו ימי שניו, or few, as written: מספר, i.e., few, like מתי מספר — one always sets his redemption according to it. Fourteen times יובל is written in the portion, corresponding to the fourteen Jubilees that were in the land until they were exiled in the days of Hosea son of Elah. And nineteen times גאולה / יגאלנו / ונגאל, corresponding to the nineteen blessings; therefore one must juxtapose גאולה to prayer."], :book :leviticus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:20:39.778941757Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}